#
# Conformance case: occurrent/boundary-mismatch
# AC: YAMATO occurrent constraint (#1081) — OccurrentBoundaryMismatch.
#
# ex:E is asserted with BOTH occurrentBoundary Open and Closed. An occurrent must
# not be both, so the violation rule must derive
# violation(E, OccurrentBoundaryMismatch). The chase seeds only from input.nq
# world facts; this program is the mirror axiom.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/occurrent/boundary-mismatch/> .

ex:E logic:occurrentBoundary logic:Open .
ex:E logic:occurrentBoundary logic:Closed .
